# MAESTRO example: LTU Festo MPS - Testing station
#
# Umbrella of this use case: the ontology header, which imports the module files under core/ and ext/.
# Single-file form: testing-merged.ttl (written by tools/merge_usecases.py).
#
# Notes carried over from the former plant.ttl, product.ttl, which this use case was split from;
# section titles and file names in them refer to those files.
#
# [plant.ttl]
# LTU FESTO MPS - TESTING STATION - PLANT (DESIGN TIME)
#
# Sources (FESTO CD/02_Testing): 648812_Manual_Testing (DE/EN 04/06
# R2.2),
# Electric_Circuit_Diagram_Testing (drawing 195781, 05.04.06),
# Pneumatic_Circuit_Diagram_Testing, 526881_Parts_list_Testing, assembly
# instructions, data sheets, operating instructions, 02_Testing_GRAFCET.
#
# I/O bits, XMA2 pins and BMKs are from the electric circuit diagram.
# Documents disagree on: 7 digital inputs in the technical data vs 8
# wired;
# BMK 3A1 = comparator (electric) and air slide (pneumatic); the COLOUR
# lamp polarity (manual: off for black; GRAFCET: on for black).
#
# STATION
#
# Material number 526881 (parts list) and manual order number 648812. The
# circuit wires 8 inputs although the technical data says 7.
#
# TECHNICAL DATA
#
# Static values from the manual's technical-data table and commissioning
# section.
#
# BILL OF MATERIALS
#
# Parts list 526881 (11.11.2002) with the components of the circuit
# diagrams below each assembly.
#
# SIGNALS (DATA POINTS)
#
# Bits, XMA2 pins and BMKs from the electric circuit diagram, pages 4-6.
# Sensor = maestro:Output / maestro:DtdlTelemetry; actuator command = maestro:Input /
# maestro:DtdlProperty.
#
# I/O PATH: SYSLINK ENDPOINTS AND DATA INTERFACES
#
# XMA2 digital, XMA3 analogue (height), XMG1 console. The URNs only name
# the connectors.
#
# MAINTENANCE
#
# Plus the cylinder and CPV notes of the operating instructions 391172
# and 165200. Displacement sensor service life 100 million operations
# (data sheet 326498).
#
# [product.ttl]
# LTU FESTO MPS - TESTING STATION - PRODUCT (RECIPES)
#
# Source: the GRAFCET function chart of the Testing station
# (02_Testing_GRAFCET.pdf).
#
# The station's control sequence as an maestro:Recipe. Steps are realised by
# the skills of plant.ttl; data bindings connect parameters declared
# there. The workpiece itself and the line recipe are in
# line/product.ttl.
#
# CONTROL SEQUENCE (GRAFCET)
#
# One maestro:PlanStep per GRAFCET step with an action; maestro:stepOrder is the
# GRAFCET step number. Empty step 6 and the flag-only steps 5 and 18 are
# folded into the transition expressions. Step 12 is drawn empty but is
# the 2 s measuring dwell, so it is kept and realised by MeasureHeight.
# Colour is not a reject criterion: it only switches the 'material'
# light.

@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .

<https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/testing> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "MAESTRO example: LTU Festo MPS - Testing station"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The Festo MPS Testing station of the LTU line: modules, parts list, I/O allocation, skills, safety and care. The GRAFCET control sequence is an HHM-Core recipe in core/recipe.ttl. Built from manual 648812, the electric and pneumatic circuit diagrams, parts list 526881, data sheets and the GRAFCET."@en ;
    owl:imports <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/shared>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/testing/core/invocation>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/testing/core/maas>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/testing/core/policy>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/testing/core/product>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/testing/core/recipe>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/testing/core/resource>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/testing/core/skill>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/testing/ext/automationml>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/testing/ext/dtdl>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/testing/ext/energy>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/testing/ext/isa95>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/testing/ext/maintenance> ;
    owl:versionIRI <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/testing/0.1.0> ;
    owl:versionInfo "0.1.0" .
